From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crunch41 <70764418+Crunch41@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:50:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Send lobby requests without Expect 100-continue

cpp-httplib adds Expect: 100-continue to any request body of 1024 bytes
or more. A room's announce reaches that at about 11 players, and the
public lobby's Caddy proxy then answers with two 100 Continue replies,
the second with headers. The client's skip loop in read_response_line
assumes an interim reply has none, fails on the header line and returns
Error::Read, which web_backend logs as "returned null" every 15 seconds.

The lobby has accepted the announce by then, so the room stays listed,
but a registration goes through the same path: a busy room the lobby
asks to register again could fail to.

Setting CPPHTTPLIB_EXPECT_100_THRESHOLD to 0 stops the header being
added. It is set on the httplib target because the library is
header-only: every file that includes it must agree on the value. The
body then goes out with the headers, which also saves a round trip.

Tested by building yuzu_room_standalone and running
tests/test_room_protocol.py, whose stand-in lobby answers Expect the way
the real lobby does; a binary without this patch fails that check.
---
 externals/CMakeLists.txt | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/externals/CMakeLists.txt b/externals/CMakeLists.txt
index 48e3b91b9fbcda01d2777f2d05f616c2c6e5fbe1..a711682131a7bde6e167ff5d9305e013b6f395b9 100644
--- a/externals/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/externals/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -69,6 +69,13 @@ if (IOS)
 endif()
 AddJsonPackage(httplib)
 
+# cpp-httplib adds Expect: 100-continue to request bodies of 1024 bytes or more, and its client
+# cannot read an interim reply that carries headers, which the public lobby's proxy sends. The
+# library is header-only, so this has to reach every file that includes it.
+if (TARGET httplib)
+    target_compile_definitions(httplib INTERFACE CPPHTTPLIB_EXPECT_100_THRESHOLD=0)
+endif()
+
 # cpp-jwt
 if (ENABLE_WEB_SERVICE OR ENABLE_UPDATE_CHECKER)
     AddJsonPackage(cpp-jwt)
